# 10. Step 9 — Build an Incident Timeline

A timeline helps connect individual events.

Example:

```text
10:01 — SSH authentication failure
10:02 — SSH authentication failure
10:03 — Successful SSH login
10:05 — sudo command executed
10:07 — New process started
10:08 — Process created network connection
10:10 — File modified
```

Timeline table:

| Time  | Event              | Evidence            |
| ----- | ------------------ | ------------------- |
| 10:01 | SSH failure        | auth.log            |
| 10:02 | SSH failure        | auth.log            |
| 10:03 | SSH success        | auth.log            |
| 10:05 | sudo activity      | sudo logs           |
| 10:07 | New process        | process information |
| 10:08 | Network connection | `ss`                |
| 10:10 | File modification  | `stat` / hash       |

### SOC mindset

Don't investigate every event separately.

Correlate:

```text
Authentication
      ↓
Privilege
      ↓
Process
      ↓
Network
      ↓
File
      ↓
Timeline
```

